Verified installation procedure with Hardware Revision C3E according to Label at the backside (Just flashing the factory.bin using the browser on the OEM upgrade page did not work at Stock Firmware Version 3.14 any more):
  - Download factory.bin and sysupgrade.bin, as both will be needed (See [[https://forum.openwrt.org/t/d-link-dir-842-c3-installation/43094/8]]) and be sure to actually rename them to these names. The default firmware seems to have problems with too long file names.
  - Connect your PC to one of the LAN-side ports and configure it to 192.168.0.2 with default gateway configured to 192.168.0.1.
  - Power the router off.
  - Press the reset button and keep it pressed while powering the router on again until the power led blinks about once per second.
  - Go to 192.168.0.1 in your browser. You'll see a quite basic firmware upload form.
  - Upload the factory.bin.
  - Do not power-cycle the router. After a while set your PC to 192.168.1.2 with default gateway 192.168.1.1.
  - Execute the following commands:
<code>
scp sysupgrade.bin root@192.168.1.1:/tmp/
ssh root@192.168.1.1
sysupgrade -v /tmp/sysupgrade.bin
ssh root@192.168.1.1
opkg update
opkg install luci
reboot
</code>

