==== Opening the case ====

<color #ed1c24>**Note:** This will void your warranty! Damage to the housing is likely!</color>

The top plate of the case is clipped into the bottom part (flaps are molded into the bottom part of the case, which snap into hinges at the top part of the case) - no screws are used.
Use a plastic wedge (e.g. a gap opener like used for mobile phone repairs), insert it at the the side of the case (take care to not lift the top too widely in a first step) and lift the gap opener up gently (assuming that the top / cover plate of the housing is facing upwards as well). By widening the bottom part of the case sideways it is less likely that the hinges of the top part (which the flaps snap into) will break when lifting the top part of the case.

Warming up the plastics with a hair dryer (or similar) may help to avoid the hinges to crack.
**Do not** use brute force - the top case's plastic can crack / break quite easily.

